<title>BURMA: Burma buys $41 mln China's sugar mill equipment.</title>
<headline>Burma buys $41 mln China's sugar mill equipment.</headline>
<dateline>RANGOON 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Burma, in a move to expand its sugar production capacity, signed a contract to buy $41 million tonnes worth of equipment from China for the construction of two sugar mills, a senior official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Myanmar (Burma) Sugarcane Enterprice (MSE) general manager U Tun Aye told Reuters that the construction of the two mills will start soon and is expected to be completed in 18 months.</p>
</text>
